@namespace Showcase.Web.Client.Pages

@page "/input-style-switcher/api"

<DemoPageHeader Title="Input Style Switcher: API" ComponentName="FaInputStyleSwitcher" DocSlug="input-style-switcher" />

<ComponentSubNav BaseRoute="/input-style-switcher" />

<p>No parameters — <code>&lt;FaInputStyleSwitcher /&gt;</code> takes nothing. It renders <code>.fa-input-style-switcher</code>, reads/writes the current input style via <code>localStorage</code> and a plain vanilla-JS call (see <code>Blazor/CLAUDE.md</code>'s "no Blazor JS interop for client-only visual state" rule), and always reflects/updates the whole page's <code>data-fa-input-style</code> attribute.</p>
